msgstr ""

#: manual/api/arithmetic.md:193
msgid "`ApproxEq` marks scalar types with an approximate comparison."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/arithmetic.md:206
msgid "`ApproxEq::approx_eq` reports whether two values are within a fixed absolute tolerance of each other."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/arithmetic.md:213
msgid "Rule"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/arithmetic.md:219
msgid "The tolerance is absolute, so it is too strict for large magnitudes and too loose for tiny ones, and the relation is not transitive. It returns `false` whenever an operand is NaN, and for an infinity compared with itself ($\\infty - \\infty$ is NaN). See the [design page](../design/arithmetic.md) for the consequences."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/arithmetic.md:240
msgid "Checked operations"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/arithmetic.md:242
msgid "The checked traits return `Result[_, ArithmeticError]` instead of a NaN or an infinity. The implementations for `Float` and `Double` delegate to the upstream `DivChecked`, `SqrtChecked` and `CompareChecked` traits; they accept an `ArithmeticContext` for interface uniformity but ignore it, because hardware binary floating point has a fixed precision."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/arithmetic.md:250
msgid "`CheckedDiv` marks scalar types with a division that reports invalid operands."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/arithmetic.md:262
